hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8174","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub, Al-Hafiz Al-San’ani, told us in Mecca from the origin of his book. Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Dabari told us, he reported Abdul Razzaq, Muammar reported, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “In At the end of time, the vision of a believer will hardly be false, and the most truthful of them is the vision of the most truthful of them in speech, and there are three types of visions: a good vision is good news. From God Almighty, and the vision that the man tells himself, and the vision is sadness from Satan, so if one of you sees a vision that he hates So do not tell it to anyone, but let him stand and pray, and the believer’s vision is one of forty-six parts of prophecy.” Abu Hurairah said: “I like shackles and hate restrictions. Chains are stability in religion.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8174 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8175","Shu’bah, on the authority of Ya’la ibn Ata’, on the authority of Waki’ ibn Adas, on the authority of his uncle Abu Razin, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The vision of the believer is part Of the forty-six parts of prophecy, it is for a flying man as long as he does not narrate it. If he narrates it, it takes place.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not mention it with the addition.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8175 - True"
"8176","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Ishaq bin Ahmad bin Mihran al-Khazzaz told us, Ishaq bin Suleiman told us Al-Razi, said: I heard Malik bin Anas, narrating on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Talha bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Zufar bin Sa’sa’ah bin Malik, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the morning prayer, he would say: “Does Did any of you see a vision tonight? “Nothing will remain after me of prophecy except a good vision.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8176 - True"
"8177","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl Al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Ishaq bin Ahmad bin Safwan Al-Bukhari told us, Yahya bin Jafar told us Al-Bukhari, Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar reported, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “A vision occurs as it is interpreted, and an example of that is like a man who has raised his leg and is waiting for when to put it down. So when he sees “One of you has a vision, so he should not narrate it except an adviser or a scholar.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8177 - True"
"8178","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad told us, al-Mukhtar ibn Fulfal told us, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, the message and prophecy have been cut off, and there is no messenger or prophet after me.” He said: This made the people sad, so he said: “But the women who bring good tidings.” So they said: Oh. Messenger of God, what are the glad tidings? He said: “The vision of a Muslim man is one of the parts of prophecy.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration on the condition of a Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8178 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8179","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Bayan Al-Muqri told us, Abdullah bin Raja told us, Harb bin Shaddad told us, On the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I was informed on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may God be pleased with him. He said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he narrated the Almighty’s saying: “For them is good news in the life of this world” [Yunus: 64]. He said: “It is the good vision that a believer sees or it is seen for him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “And it is witnessed by the hadith of Abu al-Darda’, who\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8179 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8180","It was narrated to us by Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib narrated to us, Ibn Abi Omar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Salih Al-Samman, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, who said: I asked Abu Al-Darda’, may God be pleased with him, about the words of God Almighty: “To them is good news in The life of this world} [Yunus: 64] He said: No one has asked me about it except you since I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: No one has asked me about it except you. Since it was revealed, it is the righteous vision that a Muslim sees or is shown to him.”"
"8181","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told me, Abu Issa Muhammad bin Issa told us, Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Bakr bin Mudar told us, On the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Khabab, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He says: “If one of you sees a vision that he likes, then it is from God Almighty, then let him thank God for it and narrate what he saw, and if he sees something else... This is from what he dislikes, for it is from Satan, so let him seek refuge in God from its evil and do not mention it to anyone, for it will not harm him.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8181 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8182","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Saeed bin Ufayr, and Abdullah bin Salih told us, they said: Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: O Messenger of God, I dreamed that My head was cut off while I was following him, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, rebuked him and said: “Do not tell of Satan’s tampering with you in a dream.”\n With this chain of transmission, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If one of you sees a dream and hates it, let him spit to his left.” “And let him turn away from the side he was on.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8182 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8183","Abu Al-Hasan Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Ismail bin Mahran told us, Ubi told us, Amr bin Sawad Al-Sarhi told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Abu Al-Samh told him, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “I believe the vision of the witchcraft.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8183 - True"
"8184","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad bin Al-Sammak told us, Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Shaker told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd al-A'la bin Amer, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “Whoever lies in his dream will be charged on the Day of Resurrection a ritual knot.”"
"8185","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever lies in his dream will be required to make a marriage contract between “Two hairs.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"8186","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, On the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, he said: My father told me that he heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever saw me In a dream, he saw me saying that Satan does not imitate me.” My father said: So I told Ibn Abbas about him, and said: I saw him, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned him. Al-Hasan bin Ali, so I likened him to him, and Ibn Abbas said: “He looked like him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it in this context.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8186 - True"
"8187","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Yunus bin Bukayr told us, he said: Uthman bin Abd told me. Al-Rahman, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about a paper, and she said to him: Khadija: He told the truth about you, but he died before you appeared, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I saw him in a dream wearing white clothes, even though “If he were one of the people of Hell, he would have been wearing clothing other than that.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8187 - Othman is Al-Waqqas, abandoned"
"8188","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told us, Abdullah bin Salih told me, Al-Layth told me, on the authority of Khaled bin Yazid, On the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Ata’, that Jabir bin Abdullah Al-Ansari, may God be pleased with them, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came out to us One day he said: “I saw in a dream as if Gabriel, peace and blessings be upon him, was at my head and Michael was at my feet,” he said. One of them is for its owner: Give him an example, and he said: Listen, let your ear hear, and understand the understanding of your heart. Your example and the example of your nation is like the example of a king who took He built a house in it, then he built a house in it, then he held a banquet in it, then he sent a messenger to invite the people to his meal. Some of them responded to the Messenger, and some of them responded. He left it, for God is the King, the abode is Islam, and the home is Paradise, and you, O Muhammad Messenger, whoever answers you will enter Paradise and eat whatever is in it. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8188 - True"
"8189","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Al-Wazir told us, Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari, Al-Ash’ath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said one day: “Who among you has seen a vision?” Then a man said: I saw as if a scale had descended from the sky, and you and Abu Bakr were weighed, and you preferred Abu Bakr, and Omar was weighed by Abu Bakr. Bakr, and Abu Bakr preferred, and Omar and Uthman weighed, and Omar preferred, then the scales were lifted, and I saw hatred on the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8189 - True"
"8190","Ali bin Issa Al-Hiri told me, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Abu Al-Khattab Ziyad bin Yahya Al-Jishani told us, Masada bin Al-Yasa’, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Qays ibn Ubadah, who said: I was sitting in the circle of the mosque when a man entered, and they said: This is A man from the people of Paradise prayed and left, so I followed him and said: The people said such-and-such, and he said: No one should lie or lie. He says what he does not know, and I will tell you why. I saw a vision and I related it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. I saw as if I was in a green meadow. He mentioned its spaciousness and greenery, and in the middle of the garden there was an iron pillar. Then a man came to me and said to me: Go up. I said: I cannot go up. He said: Then he brought me to a position behind me, and said: I must go up. I said: I cannot go up, so he took me up with my clothes, and when I finished, I went up to the top of the column. When there was a loop in it, I put my hand into the loop, and in the morning the loop was in my hand. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As for the garden The garden of Islam, and as for the pillar, it is the pillar of Islam, and as for the handhold, it took hold of the firmest handhold, and it remains firm on “Islam until you die.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and if the man from him had been named, it would be authentic according to their conditions.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8190 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8191","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Abu Issa Muhammad bin Issa Al-Tirmidhi told us, Sahl bin Ibrahim Al-Basri told us, Masada bin Al-Yasa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqama, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul-Rahman bin Hatib, who said: Women from The women of the believers were with Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, may God be pleased with her, and one of them said: By God, God will never punish me. I only pledged allegiance The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that I will not associate anything with God, nor steal, nor kill my children, nor bring any slander that I fabricate before me. And I have fulfilled my duty, and I will not disobey him in what is right.” And I fulfilled it. He said: So she returned to her house, and she was brought to her in her dream, and it was said to her: You are the one who is praying to God. God Almighty will not punish you, so what about your saying what does not concern you and preventing you from what does not avail you? He said: So I returned to Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and she said to her: I came in a dream and was told such-and-such, and I ask forgiveness from God and repent. To him\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8191 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8192","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Mahboub bin Fudayl, the beloved merchant in Marw, informed us. Abu Issa Muhammad bin Issa bin Surat Al-Hafiz in Tirmidh, Sahl bin Ibrahim Al-Jaudi narrated to us, Masada bin Al-Yasa narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “I saw in a dream as if three moons had fallen into my room.” So I told my dreams to Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him. When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was buried in my house, Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, said: This One of your moons, and he is the best of them. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8192 - True"
"8193","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn bin Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Indeed, I saw black sheep in a dream. Afar sheep will follow it. O Abu Bakr, cross it. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of God, the Arabs will follow you, then the non-Arabs will follow them until It was flooded, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Thus the king crossed it by magic.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8193 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8194","Abu Al-Hussein Ahmad bin Uthman bin Yahya Al-Bazzar told us, in Baghdad, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “I saw many black sheep, among which were many white sheep.” They said: What is your interpretation of this, O Messenger of God? He said: “The non-Arabs share with you in your religion and your lineage.” They said: The non-Arabs, O Messenger of God? He said: “If faith were hung on a chandelier, some of the non-Arabs would attain it and people would be happy with it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and did not “He brings him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8194 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"8195","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Musa bin Ishaq Al-Khutmi told us, Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, On the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: “The boys who came to Joseph, may the peace and blessings of God be upon him, in a vision They were only lying, and when he first saw them, he said: We were playing. Joseph said: The matter about which you were asking a fatwa has been decided. “This is an authentic hadith according to The conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not include it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8195 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8196","Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saffar told us, Al-Adl told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Amr bin Hammad told us, on the authority of Talha, Asbat bin told us Nasr, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Sabit, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: Shayban the Jew came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and said: O Muhammad, do you know the stars that Joseph saw prostrating to him? The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, remained silent about him until Gabriel, peace be upon him, came to him and told him what the Jew had asked him. He met the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. The Jew said: “O Jew, may God bless you if I told you that you would be safe?” He said: Yes, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The stars are Hadthan, and Al-Tariq, and Al-Dhabal, and Qabis, and Al-Awdan, and Al-Faliq, and Al-Nushah, and Al-Qaruh.” And the one with the cloth and the one with the branch and the jumper, Joseph saw it surrounding the covers of the sky, prostrating to him, so he related it to his father, and his father said to him: This An order, let it be dispersed, and God will bring it together, if He wills, after “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8196 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8197","Abu Al-Nadr, the jurist, and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anazi narrated to us, saying: Muadh bin Najda Al-Qurashi narrated to us, Qubaisah bin Uqba narrated to us, Sufyan, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that I saw eleven stars, he said: “The visions of the prophets were revelations.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8197 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8198","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Abu Issa Al-Tirmidhi told us, Ali bin Hajar told us, Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Salman, may God be pleased with him, who said: “There were forty years between Joseph’s vision and its interpretation.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8198 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8199","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us in Hamdan, Yahya bin Abdullah bin Mahan told us, Muhammad bin Mihran Al-Hammal told us, Abdul Rahman bin Mughraa Al-Dawsi, Al-Azhar bin Abdullah Al-Awdi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of his father, said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab met Ali Ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, and he said: O Abu Al-Hasan, the man sees a vision, and one of them is: Some of them are truthful and some of them are false. He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “There is no male or female slave who sleeps and is filled with sleep.” Unless he ascends with his spirit to the throne, then he who does not wake up without the throne, that is the vision that comes true, and he who wakes up without the throne, then that is the vision that comes true. The vision that lies\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8199 - An objectionable hadith"
"8200","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad Al-Dhuli told us, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu’tamir bin Suleiman told us, about Awf, Abu Raja told us, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “Has anyone seen Have you had a vision? He said: So whoever he wants can tell it to him, and one morning he said: “Two angels came to me tonight, one of them sat at my head and the other sat at my side.” My feet, and the one at my feet said to the one at my head: Strike like this man and like his nation. So he said: Indeed his likeness and the likeness of his nation are like the likeness of a people. On a journey, they reached the head of Mafazah, and they did not have with them any provisions with which to cross the Mafazah nor anything to return with, so while they were in that When a man came to them, wearing an ink robe, and said: What do you think, if I bring you grassy gardens and watering places, will you follow me? They said: Yes, so he set off with them and brought them to grassy gardens and watering basins, and they ate and drank and became fat, and he said to them: Did I not meet you on that? So I said to you: If I bring to you grassy gardens and refreshing places, will you follow me? They said: Yes. He said: Indeed, before you are grassy gardens than this. And a more beautiful river than this, so follow me. A group said: It is true, by God, we will follow. A group said: We are satisfied with this. We will establish it upon it. An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8200 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8201","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Bishr bin Musa Al-Asadi told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa Al-Ashhab told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ammar bin Ammar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in what a sleeper sees in the middle of the day. Ash'ath was brought to dust with a vial of blood, so I said: O Prophet of God, what is this? He said: “This is the blood of Hussein and his companions. I have been collecting it since that day.” He said: “So that day was counted and they found him killed before that.” “One day.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8201 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8202","Abu Al-Hussein Ali bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Shaybani told us in Kufa, Ahmad bin Hazim Al-Ghafari told us, Khalid bin Mukhlid told us. Al-Qatwani, said: Musa bin Yaqoub Al-Zuma’i told me, Hashim bin Hashim bin Utbah bin Abi Waqqas told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Wahb bin Zamaa said: Umm Salamah, may God be pleased with her, told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lay down to sleep one night. So he woke up and was confused, then he lay down and fell asleep, then he woke up and was confused, without what I saw of him the first time, then he lay down and woke up and in He had red soil in his hand and was kissing it. I said: What is this soil, O Messenger of God? He said: “Gabriel, peace and blessings be upon him, told me that this man will be killed in the land of Iraq - for Al-Hussein - so I said to Gabriel: Show me the soil of the land.” With which he is killed, this is its soil. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8202 - This was according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8203","Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Qattan informed us in Baghdad, Abd al-Karim ibn al-Haytham al-Dir’aquli informed us, Abu Al-Yaman, Shuaib bin Abi Hamza reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Husayn, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God have mercy on him. On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I saw in a dream as if I had two bracelets of gold on my hands, and I became concerned about them, so it was revealed Until I blew them, so I blew them and they flew, so I treated them as liars who would emerge after me. He said: One of them has Musaylimah, the companion of Al-Yamama, and Al-Adani, the companion of Ansa’ “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8203 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8204","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ubayy told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Yazid, on the authority of Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ The greatest slander is when a man slanders his own eyes, saying: I saw and he did not see, or slanders his parents, or says: He heard me but he did not hear me. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8204 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
